  "comments": "House of Windsor (1917 to date), Elizabeth II (1952-2022), Pre-decimal issues (1953-70).<br /><br />\r\nThe original weight of these coins was 2/11 troy ounce (87.3 grains). Under the Coinage Act of 1946, the composition changed from .500 silver to .750 copper/.250 nickel but the weight remained at 87.3 grains.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">1955 reverse die varieties:</span><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Rev C</span> D of DEF at a bead, F of DEF between beads, both quatrefoils between beads, 2nd I in SHILLING at a bead;<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Rev D</span> D of DEF between beads, F of DEF to left of bead, left quatrefoil at a bead, right quatrefoil to left of bead, 2nd I in SHILLING between beads;<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5cc5766e62f62.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5cc5766e62f62.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">1959 reverse die varieties:</span><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Type 1</span> All 3 ornaments touch the baseline;<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Type 2</span> Ornaments 1 &amp; 3 away from baseline;<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5cc5c7104e3ba.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5cc5c7104e3ba.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\nImages above are reproduced with kind permission of Declan Magee Coins and Numista member Sjoelund.<br /><br />\r\nThe 1970-dated proof strikes were issued as part of the &#039;Last Sterling&#039; mint set which comprised<br />\r\nhalf crown to halfpenny and were produced over the course of several years:<br />\r\n01/04/71-31/03/72 = 69,763<br />\r\n01/04/72-31/03/73 = 586,554<br />\r\n01/04/73-31/03/74 = 74,293<br />\r\n01/04/74-31/03/75 = 19,814",
